  <h3 class="close">About The Webmaster</h3>
  <p class="closep">Hello, I'm Michael Tisdale: the Bolex Collector, or Webmaster, 
    or "the guy who designed this site". I live in Atlanta, GA, with my wife, 
    two cats and a collection of old movie cameras (among other things). </p>
  <p>That's me in the photo above. It was taken several years ago, but I'd rather 
    be behind a camera than in front of it, so that'll have to do. Oh, I'm squinting 
    there, not scowling -- even though it isn't fun being a target for objects 
    hurled by drunken men on parade floats. </p>
  <p>This site is dedicated to my obsession with collecting and using Bolex cameras. 
    Although I've collected many types of still and movie cameras from different 
    manufacturers since 1991, I have a particular interest in Paillard Bolex. 
  </p>
  <p>Over the years, I've discovered others who also share my interest in collecting 
    and filming with classic cameras; both as a hobby and professionally. I created 
    this website in 2005, to share information with other Bolex enthusiasts. </p>
  <p>I don't collect cameras as much as I used to; I only keep what I use. I enjoy 
    time-lapse and scenic cinematography, and prefer spring-wound cameras over 
    anything that uses a battery. If you have comments or questions, or would 
    just like to discuss Bolex cameras, I look forward to your <a href="contact.html">email</a> 
  </p>
